BSP-Yocto-NXP-i.MX8MP-FPSC-ALPHA1         2025-08-11
====================================================

- Linux NXP Vendor Kernel v6.6.52-2.2.0-phy20 (based on NXP tag lf-6.6.52-2.2.0)
- U-boot v2024.04-2.0.0-phy21 (based on NXP tag lf-6.6.52-2.2.0)
- Yocto 5.0.11 (Scarthgap)
- Qt 6.7
- OP-TEE 4.4
- RAUC 1.14

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt6demo-image:
  * imx8mp-libra-fpsc-1

- phytec-vision-image:
  * imx8mp-libra-fpsc-1

- phytec-headless-image:
  * imx8mp-libra-fpsc-1

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04 64-bit

New Features:
-------------
- Boot via USB serial download (uuu)
- Boot from e.MMC
- Boot from SD card
- Ethernet Boot support
- U-Boot standard boot (https://docs.u-boot.org/en/v2024.04/develop/bootstd.html#u-boot-standard-boot)
- Overlay handling support
- Debug UART support
- Watchdog support
- GBit Ethernet support (SoM + Carrier board)
- i2c EEPROM
- i2c LEDs
- i2c RTC support
- i2c GPIO expander
- USB 3.0 Host support
- USB C peripheral support (device only)
- PCIe support
- RS232 (no flow control)
- CANfd
- LVDS display on board support AC209
- GPU support
- SPI NOR flash (no booting possible yet)
- Camera support
    * VM-016 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-017 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
    * VM-020 phyCAM-M / phyCAM-L
- ISP support

Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
- RS232 hardware flow control is not working due to swapped pins on SoM
- Video in Qt6 Demo hangs for few seconds before plays correctly using
  hardware acceleration
